+    This paper presented a degradation-aware framework for planning shared ESSs at TN--DN interface nodes. Planning is formulated as a two-stage stochastic program whose first stage selects a single, discrete investment plan and whose recourse is the coordinated TSO--DSO operation of that plan, a nonconvex problem with AC network models and the ageing of the storage over the horizon. Candidate plans are proposed by a derivative-free search over the lattice of commercial unit sizes and evaluated by consensus-ADMM coordination with a dedicated shared-ESS agent. Because the recourse is nonconvex, the method claims no optimality certificate; instead, each evaluation behind a reported comparison has a stated stopping status --- certified by an explicit rule, uncertified with its error bar, or, at the multi-scenario instance, stopped by the production exit with its remaining movement measured --- and every planning comparison is reported with the resolution at which it is decided.
